{"adverse_evidence": null, "authority": "authority/source/descent.tex", "authority_sha256": "49483B3BCB36427A607A8227F4EA67730FCDDF1EECCB8E992CA61915ACE3B31D", "class": "source_defect", "locus": "descent.tex:8708,8727", "operations": [{"class": "source_defect", "declared_line_occurrences": 1, "end_byte_exclusive": 326864, "file_occurrences": 2, "line": 8708, "old_bytes": 32, "old_sha256": "2458B45BDE730044CD50A8033274CD0D6A7B0FC1A5BBB6FA476F36922AF92B89", "old_text": "The first morphism has a section", "operation_id": "MC-STK-ERR-1427-OP1", "origin": "producer_packet_and_independent_adjudication", "producer_id": "DESCENT-038", "producer_operation_id": "DESCENT-038-OP1", "replacement_bytes": 35, "replacement_sha256": "1CFD5161D368A8102F657417845E34901F5D00C53B473E24F93392B2E6E1415D", "replacement_text": "The first morphism has a retraction", "source": "descent.tex", "source_end_line": 8708, "source_start_line": 8708, "stable_id": "MC-STK-ERR-1427", "start_byte": 326832}, {"class": "source_defect", "declared_line_occurrences": 1, "end_byte_exclusive": 327634, "file_occurrences": 2, "line": 8727, "old_bytes": 32, "old_sha256": "2458B45BDE730044CD50A8033274CD0D6A7B0FC1A5BBB6FA476F36922AF92B89", "old_text": "The first morphism has a section", "operation_id": "MC-STK-ERR-1427-OP2", "origin": "producer_packet_and_independent_adjudication", "producer_id": "DESCENT-038", "producer_operation_id": "DESCENT-038-OP2", "replacement_bytes": 35, "replacement_sha256": "1CFD5161D368A8102F657417845E34901F5D00C53B473E24F93392B2E6E1415D", "replacement_text": "The first morphism has a retraction", "source": "descent.tex", "source_end_line": 8727, "source_start_line": 8727, "stable_id": "MC-STK-ERR-1427", "start_byte": 327602}], "payload": "payload/descent.tex", "producer_aliases": [], "producer_id": "DESCENT-038", "producer_ids": ["DESCENT-038"], "proof": "In each factorization X -> X times_S X' -> X', the first arrow is the graph of f and the first projection is its retraction; the graph is a section, but is not thereby a morphism having a section. Both repeated proofs require 'has a retraction' to invoke the equivalence lemma in the correct categorical direction.", "schema": "mathematics-commons-stacks-source-map/v2", "source": "descent.tex", "unit_id": "MC-STK-ERR-1427"}
{"adverse_evidence": null, "authority": "authority/source/descent.tex", "authority_sha256": "49483B3BCB36427A607A8227F4EA67730FCDDF1EECCB8E992CA61915ACE3B31D", "class": "source_defect", "locus": "descent.tex:8718", "operations": [{"class": "source_defect", "declared_line_occurrences": 1, "end_byte_exclusive": 327328, "file_occurrences": 1, "line": 8718, "old_bytes": 100, "old_sha256": "900D22A91B83CB2C1AE2452B75B4F36B04F6E9194F76CA5FB9F8425D2AD17C66", "old_text": "Assume $\\{X \\to S\\}$ is an fpqc covering (for example if $f$ is\nsurjective, flat and quasi-compact).", "operation_id": "MC-STK-ERR-1428-OP1", "origin": "producer_packet_and_independent_adjudication", "producer_id": "DESCENT-039", "producer_operation_id": "DESCENT-039-OP1", "replacement_bytes": 106, "replacement_sha256": "7943C5EB63E159498CD690268051A7E9F23BC2954E082A1029D85261A55F24D4", "replacement_text": "Assume $\\{X \\to S\\}$ is an fpqc covering (for example if $X \\to S$ is\nsurjective, flat and quasi-compact).", "source": "descent.tex", "source_end_line": 8719, "source_start_line": 8718, "stable_id": "MC-STK-ERR-1428", "start_byte": 327228}], "payload": "payload/descent.tex", "producer_aliases": [], "producer_id": "DESCENT-039", "producer_ids": ["DESCENT-039"], "proof": "The hypothesis is that X -> S is an fpqc covering. Surjectivity, flatness, and quasi-compactness of the different morphism f:X->X' do not imply that hypothesis, so the parenthetical sufficient condition must refer to X -> S. The full two-line guard avoids changing the valid f-based parenthetical at lines 8565--8566.", "schema": "mathematics-commons-stacks-source-map/v2", "source": "descent.tex", "unit_id": "MC-STK-ERR-1428"}
{"adverse_evidence": null, "authority": "authority/source/descent.tex", "authority_sha256": "49483B3BCB36427A607A8227F4EA67730FCDDF1EECCB8E992CA61915ACE3B31D", "class": "source_defect", "locus": "descent.tex:8766", "operations": [{"class": "source_defect", "declared_line_occurrences": 1, "end_byte_exclusive": 328870, "file_occurrences": 1, "line": 8766, "old_bytes": 32, "old_sha256": "01C617FC35982FD70EFDF745496DCAB4E87313D6F9F0797CE8B174581A6B46A0", "old_text": "via the morphism $g_{\\alpha(i)}$", "operation_id": "MC-STK-ERR-1429-OP1", "origin": "producer_packet_and_independent_adjudication", "producer_id": "DESCENT-040", "producer_operation_id": "DESCENT-040-OP1", "replacement_bytes": 22, "replacement_sha256": "5A6BE3A3B8611A67A47CB05602BBF723B235F4A8BE049170916DFDFD1D707E49", "replacement_text": "via the morphism $g_i$", "source": "descent.tex", "source_end_line": 8766, "source_start_line": 8766, "stable_id": "MC-STK-ERR-1429", "start_byte": 328838}], "payload": "payload/descent.tex", "producer_aliases": [], "producer_id": "DESCENT-040", "producer_ids": ["DESCENT-040"], "proof": "The family morphisms are g_i:U_i->V_{alpha(i)} indexed by i in I, while alpha(i) lies in J and does not index a g-map; the ith coproduct component is therefore mapped by g_i.", "schema": "mathematics-commons-stacks-source-map/v2", "source": "descent.tex", "unit_id": "MC-STK-ERR-1429"}
